// RHYTHM BANKRUPTCY — FIRE SALE — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// RHYTHM BANKRUPTCY as nu-disco — a game alternate of rhythm, selectable from the dev
// menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces the live song.
// 
// Everything must go. The band is in the next room when the cabinet screen opens — a
// filter-house loop, octave bass and clav through a shut lowpass — and the filter
// opens bar by bar into a disco band. The original's octave bass was always a disco
// bass; here it is one. A talkbox sings: the original's sparse call figure (C G G A E)
// in the verse, over a violin section running the ARP (cycle one) in sixteenths, and
// the POPCORN HOOK (cycle two) in the chorus, doubled by a grand, with the brass
// answering in the hook's own beat of nothing. The bed is the original's doo-wop
// turnaround, a chord every half bar, cell for cell. The break drops to congas and
// bass and re-harmonises the hook as an Andalusian cadence (Am G F E7sus4); the last
// chorus is a whole step up, the lift rhythm.js makes, with both figures at once.
// 
//   1–4    intro — the loop through a shut filter (the cabinet-screen loop)
//   5–8    the filter opens a bar at a time; violins, tambourine, riser, fill
//   9–16   verse — violins on the arp, the talkbox on the call figure
//   17–32  chorus — talkbox and grand on the Popcorn hook, brass in the rests
//   33–40  disco break — congas, cowbell, bass; the hook over Am G F E7sus4
//   41–44  build — the hook held in C over Dm7 C/E Fmaj7 A7; roll, riser
//   45–60  chorus two (D) — hook, brass and the violins' arp together
//   61–64  everything must go — the band leaves a lane a bar; the loop returns to bar 9
// 
// THE BEAT CABINET'S CLOCK IS KEPT. 124 BPM straight, 4/4, phrases of four bars from
// bar 1, the kick on every quarter of every bar and never filtered — the beat charts
// are laid off Audio.songBeat() mod 16. The loop is bars 9–64: 56 bars, a whole
// number of 16-beat chart loops.
// 
// 64 bars at 124. Written by work/local/_rhythm-remix-fire-sale.mjs through
// work/local/_remix-lib.mjs; re-running it rewrites this file.
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
// about the song up here, where they survive.
